'''The Forbidden Reach''' (originally the '''Reach''')<ref>''[[World of Warcraft: War of the Scaleborn]]''</ref> is an island located off the coast of the [[Dragon Isles]]. It was fashioned by [[Deathwing|Neltharion]] the Earth-Warder to serve as a training ground for his ultimate soldiers, the [[dracthyr]]. But in the aftermath of a terrible battle, the island has lain dormant and abandoned for ages until the return of an ancient enemy causes the dracthyr to stir.<ref>[https://worldofwarcraft.com/en-us/news/23876527/the-story-so-far-take-wing-through-time-with-the-dragon-aspects The Story So Far: Take Wing Through Time with the Dragon Aspects]</ref>

The [[dracthyr starting experience]] takes place in a special version of this zone at level 10 (originally 58).

Until [[patch 10.0.7]] when the zone was re-opened, when a player visited the Forbidden Reach outside of the evoker starting experience by flying from the mainland Dragon Isles, they were struck by lightning until they died.<ref>{{ref web|url=https://twitter.com/MrGMYT/status/1559988092408406016|title=Tweet by MrGM|quote=When you head back to the Forbidden Reach (Dracthyr Starting Zone) on a regular Character on the Dragon Isles, you can't mount your Dragonriding mount and are constantly attacked by lightening until you die|date=2022-08-17|author=MrGM}}</ref>

==Description==
[[File:Dracthyr in magical stasis.png|thumb|Beneath the surface, legions of dracthyr were in magical stasis for thousands of years.]]
The Forbidden Reach was once fashioned by [[Deathwing|Neltharion the Earth-Warder]] himself to be the secret training grounds of the [[black dragonflight]] and of its [[Dracthyr|would-be ultimate soldiers]]. The Reach has since descended into a broken and deserted landscape, lost to the ravages of time. Those few dragons who remember the island know that it is taboo to visit, as it is a place where something dreadful fell. Those who have braved the shores found little of consequence in this cauldron-like caldera apart from a shattered landscape and nature-claimed ruins half buried by magma. Deep beneath the surface, vast underground chambers contain legions of dracthyr, resting in magical stasis for thousands of years.<ref>[https://worldofwarcraft.com/en-gb/news/23832633/dragonflight-zone-preview-the-forbidden-reach Dragonflight Zone Preview: The Forbidden Reach]</ref>

[[Malygos]] once assigned three [[blue dragon]]s ([[Andesigos]], [[Lapisagos]] and [[Venagosa]]) and loyal [[drakonid]] troops, known as the [[Spellsworn]], to ensure the dracthyr stayed locked underground forever.<ref>[[Report: Infestation]]</ref>

==Quests==
{{main|Dracthyr starting experience|Forbidden Reach storyline}}

Quests in the Forbidden Reach play out as part of the [[dracthyr starting experience]] for [[evoker]]s, leading them to explore much of the island as well as kick off the story of the [[Dragonflight campaign]]. Dracthyr of other classes also start here, but depart for the main cities after just a few minutes.

Later, players return in [[patch 10.0.7]] for the [[Forbidden Reach storyline]].

